  "title": "The C prop rock",
  "verdict": "refuted",
  "headline": "The 'C' on the Apollo 16 rock is absent from every scan of the original flight film and from three independent print scans; it exists only in one print generation, where a high-resolution re-scan resolves it as a ~0.9 mm curled fiber (with a visible tail and a second hair in the same crop) lying on top of the film grain.",
